From: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 22:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: invalidate stale PPE vifs on recovery

Firmware recovery destroys and recreates the datapath, including the PPE
direct-switch node and its VP profile table.  The mac80211 vif objects can
survive that transition, so their cached VP identifiers must not be used
with the new table.

Invalidate the per-vif PPE state while the active vif list is still
available in core_halt().  Also recover during attach if an interface with
stale state reaches the new, empty profile table due to a different
callback order.  Do not release the cached bank in either path: the old
bank table is destroyed by datapath teardown and may already have been
reinitialized when the attach fallback runs.

Assisted-by: Codex:GPT-5.6-sol
Signed-off-by: Yanghan Ye <yyh94306@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c |  8 +++++++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c  | 13 +++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1449,6 +1449,7 @@ void ath12k_core_halt(struct ath12k *ar)
 {
 	struct list_head *pos, *n;
 	struct ath12k_base *ab = ar->ab;
+	struct ath12k_link_vif *arvif;
 
 	lockdep_assert_wiphy(ath12k_ar_to_hw(ar)->wiphy);
 
@@ -1468,8 +1469,13 @@ void ath12k_core_halt(struct ath12k *ar)
 	synchronize_rcu();
 
 	spin_lock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
-	list_for_each_safe(pos, n, &ar->arvifs)
+	list_for_each_safe(pos, n, &ar->arvifs) {
+		arvif = list_entry(pos, struct ath12k_link_vif, list);
+		arvif->ppe_vp = -1;
+		arvif->ppe_vp_profile = -1;
+		arvif->ppe_search_idx = -1;
 		list_del_init(pos);
+	}
 	spin_unlock_bh(&ar->data_lock);
 
 	idr_init(&ar->txmgmt_idr);
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/ppe.c
@@ -985,8 +985,17 @@ int ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_attach(struct ath1
 	if (vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_AP &&
 	    vif->type != NL80211_IFTYPE_STATION)
 		return 0;
-	if (arvif->ppe_vp >= 64)
-		return ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_program(arvif);
+	if (arvif->ppe_vp >= 64) {
+		ret = ath12k_ppe_ds_vif_program(arvif);
+		if (!ret)
+			return 0;
+		if (ret != -ENOENT)
+			return ret;
+
+		arvif->ppe_vp = -1;
+		arvif->ppe_vp_profile = -1;
+		arvif->ppe_search_idx = -1;
+	}
 
 	vp = qcom_ppe_ds_vp_alloc(ppe->node, wdev->netdev);
 	if (vp < 0)
-- 
